combined data center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027, the aggregate AI-infrastructure spend Nvidia projects and on which its GPU demand depends?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditure for calendar 2027, as disclosed in their full-year results.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"new_theses\": [],\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"E1\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, with the GPUs not driving the increase; the bank estimates NVIDIA will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n    \"source_passages\": [\n     \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation. The GPUs themselves are not the driver of the increase. The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\"\n    ],\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"E2\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND; memory rose to 25–30% of the bill of materials on the VR200 from 5–10% on the GB200, while the GPU's share fell from about 63% to 51%.\",\n    \"source_passages\": [\n     \"The memory line is where the cost concentrates. Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 te